_1h_input_tokens": 5052}, "output_tokens": 3, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-29T08:58:19.087Z", "request_id": "req_011CgWFZUBc8mqm3K3rqRq12", "thinking_duration_ms": 14352}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 0}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 1, "content_block": {"type": "text", "text": ""}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgWFZUUDFppgRAEBa6uwb", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I traced the plans by hand without running anything, so this ranking is approximate. My best half is 6, 1, 4 and 3.\n\n1. **Fixed order cost.** Daily ordering pays 28 × 42 = 1,176. Ordering every other day pays 14 × 42 = 588. That is 588 cheaper.\n2. **Cost of the extra stock.** Ordering every other day means holding about one day's demand for one more night. That is roughly 40 × 0.7 + 42 × 0.2 ≈ 36 per two-day cycle, or about 510 over the month. It saves more than it costs. Pooling two days' demand also smooths out the randomness a little. So plans 6, 4 and 1 come out ahead of the daily plans.\n3. **How much to order.** For good 0, a missed unit costs 14 (lost margin 6 plus penalty 8). A leftover unit costs 11 plus storage. For good 1 the figures are 10 versus 5. Demand also averages about 4.6% above forecast. So the best order is about 1.1–1.2 × forecast:\n   - **Plan 6** (~1.1 × forecast, every other day) is the best balance.\n   - **Plan 1** (~1.2 × forecast) is good, but on day 22, 112 + 148 = 260 units arrive on top of leftovers. Some good 1 will overflow the 292-unit warehouse.\n   - **Plan 4** (~1.0 × forecast) orders a bit too little, but the lower fixed cost keeps it in the top half.\n4. **Every three days (plan 5).** It pays the least fixed cost (420), but deliveries of up to 268 units plus leftovers will overflow. Storage and write-offs of good 1 (5-day shelf life) will also cost more. I expect it in the bottom half.\n5. **Daily plans.** Plan 3 (~1.1 × forecast for both goods) is the best of them. Plan 2 (~1.2) over-orders. Plan 0 orders good 1 at exactly the forecast. Plan 7 orders exactly the forecast for both goods, which is too little given the cost asymmetry.\n\nThe weakest call is plan 3 versus plan 2. Those two are close, and I gave plan 3 only slightly better than even odds."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 5052, "cache_read_input_tokens": 886, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 5052}, "output_tokens": 3, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-29T08:58:27.308Z", "request_id": "req_011CgWFZUBc8mqm3K3rqRq12"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01AJRqQ9ensZw893Fn4sWNJJ", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgWFZUUDFppgRAEBa6uwb", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01AJRqQ9ensZw893Fn4sWNJJ", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {"p": [0.3, 0.62, 0.42, 0.52, 0.6, 0.3, 0.72, 0.2]}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cach